cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "Fuel-optimal convex guidance versus a braking heuristic for tower capture"
abstract: >-
  A simulation study of the terminal phase of a Super Heavy booster tower catch. A convex
  model-predictive controller (lossless convexification, second-order cone program) and an
  engineered braking-profile controller fly identical dispersed landing burns with shared
  sensing, actuation, estimation, terminal descent and abort logic. Includes a Monte Carlo
  campaign, engine-failure, crosswind and capture-basin studies, an engine-out braking
  reserve, independent verification of the guidance, and an interactive 3D replay.
type: software
